{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SITE HEADER — tablet and desktop
  REFERENCE §7.1 · design/SiteHeader.dc.html
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  A 64px bar, two mega panels, one toolbar pill, one identity control. Hidden below
  768px, where the phone has the app bar and the tab bar instead.

  ── WHY THIS IS A PARTIAL AND NOT PART OF `layout/nav.twig` ─────────────────

  It was, and that made `nav.twig` two things: the desktop header AND the phone
  chrome — tab bar, Menu sheet, language prompt — because the legacy layout needs
  both from one include.

  The moment a page on the redesign shell wanted a header, that bundle came with it:
  a tab bar on a FLOW page, which §7.3 says has none, and a second copy of the Menu
  sheet beside the one `layout/shell.twig` already mounts. Two elements carrying
  `data-ag-menu-sheet` means the opener finds the first and the tab bar's button
  appears dead — the same duplicate-id fault the search palette had, which was
  measured on the rendered page rather than reasoned about.

  So: this is the header. `layout/nav.twig`, which included it and added the phone
  chrome for the pages on the old layout, was destroyed with them on 3 Oct 2026
  (docs/handoff/DESTROYED.md). A shell page includes THIS and gets a header and
  nothing else; the shell mounts the phone sheets, and `SiteHeaderTest` holds that
  the header mounts neither.

  ── THERE IS NO GREEN BUTTON IN THIS HEADER ─────────────────────────────────

  §6.1: green is THE primary action INSIDE the page. A green pill in the chrome is on
  screen beside every page's own call to action and wins, so the page's real action
  becomes the second loudest thing on it — on every page. The signed-out control is
  an outlined pill, and `SiteHeaderTest` asserts it in both signed-in states.

  ── THE MEGA CONTROLLER IS THE ONE THAT WAS ALREADY HERE ────────────────────

  Kept deliberately (phase §7.1: "Keep the repo's `data-ag-mega*` controller"). It
  carries three fixes that are invisible until they are missing — per-trigger handlers
  bound after DOMContentLoaded so no document listener can re-close the panel on the
  same click, hover-open gated on a fine pointer, and Esc closing everything.
#}
{% set _p = gates_page|default('') %}
{% set _ini = member_name ? (member_name|split(' ')|map(w => w|first)|join|upper|slice(0,2)) : 'AG' %}

{% if announcement_text %}
<div class="ag-announce ag-scope" role="region" aria-label="Announcement">
  <span class="ag-announce__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span>{{ announcement_text }}</span>
  {% if announcement_url %}<a href="{{ announcement_url }}">{{ announcement_cta|default('Learn more →') }}</a>{% endif %}
  <button class="ag-announce__x" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss" data-ag-do="dismiss-parent">×</button>
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="ag-head" data-ag-head>
  <header class="ag-head__bar" role="banner">

    <a class="ag-logo" href="/" aria-label="Africa GATES home">
      <img src="{{ asset('/assets/img/logo-mark.png') }}" width="32" height="32" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
      <span><b>Africa</b><i>GATES</i></span>
    </a>

    {# ── TWO TOP LINKS, AND THE WHOLE SITE BEHIND THEM ────────────────────
       The lists are §7.1's, not the DC's: `SiteHeader.dc.html` puts seven items
       under Explore including Leaderboard and Shop and no Status, and REFERENCE
       §0 puts the phase file above the DC. Recorded in GAPS.md §9.3.

       Every tile's tint is a TOKEN pair rather than the DC's eight hexes — see
       GAPS.md §9.1, and `.ag-tint--*` in components/chrome.css for the measurements.

       Explore carries a SEVENTH item, Results, and that is not a loosening of §7.1.
       Results is in neither of the phase file's two lists, and `PublicResultsTest`
       exists because of exactly what that costs: the page was built, the Pulse and
       the emails linked it, and nobody browsing the site could reach a decided
       award. A spec that omits a destination does not make it optional. GAPS.md §9.8.

       And a comment cannot go INSIDE the array below — Twig lexes a comment only
       between tags, never inside an expression, and it answers a stray hash in an
       array literal with a SyntaxError naming a backtick.

       Nor may a comment CONTAIN a comment's closing brace-hash. Writing that pair
       here to illustrate the rule ended the comment on the spot and printed the
       remaining four lines of prose into the page, above the header, on every
       screen of the site. Name the characters; do not type them. #}
    <nav class="ag-head__top" aria-label="Primary">
      {% for m in [
        {k:'participate', label:'Participate', items:[
          {href:'/nominate',         label:'Nominate',           sub:'Put someone forward in under 90 seconds', tint:'green',   d:'M12 5v14M5 12h14'},
          {href:'/vote',             label:'Vote',               sub:'One verified voter, one vote per category', tint:'green', d:'M4 12.5 9 17.5 20 6.5'},
          {href:'/awards',           label:'Awards',             sub:'Every award, edition and category',       tint:'gold',    d:'M5 16 3 6l5 4 4-6 4 6 5-4-2 10z'},
          {href:'/giving',           label:'Giving',             sub:'Back the programmes behind the awards',   tint:'live',    d:'M20.8 4.6a5.5 5.5 0 0 0-7.8 0L12 5.6l-1-1a5.5 5.5 0 0 0-7.8 7.8L12 21l8.8-8.6a5.5 5.5 0 0 0 0-7.8Z'},
          {href:'/account/register', label:'Register a profile', sub:'Join the continental registry, free',     tint:'gold',    d:'M16 11a4 4 0 1 0-8 0M3 21a9 9 0 0 1 18 0'},
          {href:'/integrity',        label:'Integrity Center',   sub:'How voting, judging and audits work',     tint:'neutral', d:'M12 2.4l7.6 2.7v5.8c0 4.7-3.1 8.3-7.6 10-4.5-1.7-7.6-5.3-7.6-10V5.1z'}
        ]},
        {k:'explore', label:'Explore', items:[
          {href:'/discover', label:'Discover',     sub:'People, organisations and awards',      tint:'neutral', d:'M11 4a7 7 0 1 0 0 14 7 7 0 0 0 0-14ZM20 20l-3.6-3.6'},
          {href:'/pulse',    label:'Pulse',        sub:'Posts and live moments',                tint:'live',    d:'M5 3h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2ZM10 8.5l5 3.5-5 3.5z'},
          {href:'/events',   label:'Events',       sub:'Ceremonies, livestreams and sessions',  tint:'green',   d:'M4 5h16v15H4zM4 10h16M9 3v4M15 3v4'},
          {href:'/legacy',   label:'Legacy Vault', sub:'Every edition, permanently archived',   tint:'gold',    d:'M4 8h16v12H4zM2 4h20v4H2z'},
          {href:'/blog',     label:'Blog',         sub:'Stories and methodology notes',         tint:'neutral', d:'M4 5h16M4 10h16M4 15h10'},
          {href:'/results',  label:'Results',      sub:'Every award decided, with the working shown', tint:'gold', d:'M5 16 3 6l5 4 4-6 4 6 5-4-2 10z'},
          {href:'/status',   label:'Status',       sub:'Whether every part of this is working', tint:'neutral', d:'M3 12h4l3-7 4 14 3-7h4'}
        ]}
      ] %}
        <div class="ag-mega-wrap" data-ag-mega>
          <button type="button" class="ag-head__link" data-ag-mega-trigger
                  aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false">{{ m.label }}
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M13.8 7.2 10 11 6.2 7.2 5 8.3l5 5 5-5z"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="ag-mega" data-ag-mega-panel role="menu" aria-label="{{ m.label }}">
            <div class="ag-mega__grid">
              {% for i in m.items %}
                <a class="ag-mega__item" role="menuitem" href="{{ i.href }}">
                  <span class="ag-icon-tile ag-icon-tile--mega ag-tint--{{ i.tint }}" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg width="19" height="19" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                         stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                      <path d="{{ i.d }}"></path></svg>
                  </span>
                  <span class="ag-mega__txt"><b>{{ i.label }}</b><span>{{ i.sub }}</span></span>
                </a>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </nav>

    <span class="ag-head__gap"></span>

    <div class="ag-head__end">

      {# ── THE TOOLBAR PILL ──────────────────────────────────────────────
         Three controls in one 40px pill with hairline dividers. `role="toolbar"`
         is a claim about arrow-key navigation between the three, which
         `header.js` implements — a toolbar that only answers Tab is a toolbar
         in name. #}
      <div class="ag-tools" role="toolbar" aria-label="Search, accessibility and language">
        <button type="button" class="ag-tools__b" data-ag-search-open
                aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false"
                aria-label="Search Africa GATES. Shortcut: press the slash key">
          <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
               stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
            <path d="m20 20-3.6-3.6" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg>
        </button>
        <span class="ag-tools__div" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <button type="button" class="ag-tools__b ag-tools__aa" data-ag-pop="aa"
                aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false"
                aria-label="Display and reading">Aa</button>
        <span class="ag-tools__div" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {# The CODE, not the name: two letters fit a 40px pill and eight names do
           not. The accessible label carries the language in full, so nobody is
           asked to know that "ig" is Igbo. #}
        <button type="button" class="ag-tools__b ag-tools__lang" data-ag-pop="lang"
                aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false"
                aria-label="Language: {{ lang_name() }}. Choose another">
          <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
               stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
            <path d="M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 2.7 3.8 5.7 3.8 9s-1.3 6.3-3.8 9c-2.5-2.7-3.8-5.7-3.8-9S9.5 5.7 12 3Z"></path></svg>
          <span>{{ lang()|upper }}</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      {# Rendered on shop routes, and revealed by `header.js` anywhere the basket
         is not empty. The basket lives in this browser's own storage, so the
         server cannot know: shipping the button hidden and letting the page that
         CAN read it decide is the only arrangement that does not either hide a
         full basket or show an empty one. No subtotal — §7.1. #}
      {% set _shop = _p starts with 'shop' %}
      <a class="ag-head__cart" href="/shop/cart" data-ag-cart
         {% if not _shop %}hidden{% endif %} aria-label="Your basket">
        <svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M5.5 8h13l-1 12h-11z"></path><path d="M9 8V7a3 3 0 0 1 6 0v1"></path></svg>
        <span class="ag-head__cartn" data-ag-cart-n hidden></span>
      </a>

      {% if is_member %}
        <a class="ag-head__av" href="/account" aria-label="Your account">{{ _ini }}</a>
      {% else %}
        {# Outlined, never green — see the note at the top of this file. #}
        <a class="ag-head__signin" href="/account/login">Sign in</a>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </header>

  {# ── THE TWO POPOVERS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Both hang from `top:70px` under the bar. Display & reading is the SAME
     partial the phone sheet and the Menu use, because three copies of seven
     switches is how the halves of a setting come to disagree. #}
  <div class="ag-pop ag-pop--aa" data-ag-pop-panel="aa" role="dialog"
       aria-label="Display and reading" inert>
    {% include 'partials/display-reading.twig' with { uid: 'aa' } %}
  </div>

  <div class="ag-pop ag-pop--lang" data-ag-pop-panel="lang" role="menu"
       aria-label="Language" inert>
    {% for l in languages() %}
      {# A link, because following it navigates and the middleware stores the
         choice — so the language menu works with scripting off. #}
      <a class="ag-pop__lang" role="menuitem" href="{{ lang_url(l.code) }}" lang="{{ l.code }}"
         {{ l.code == lang() ? 'aria-current="true"' : '' }}>
        {{ l.name }}<i>{{ l.code|upper }}</i>
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>

<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
(function(){
  function init(){
    // ── MEGAS — the controller phase §7.1 says to keep ─────────────────────
    //
    // Direct per-trigger handlers bound (after DOMContentLoaded) to the FINAL
    // elements, with stopPropagation so no other document click handler can
    // immediately re-close the panel. A click outside any wrap closes all.
    var wraps = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.ag-mega-wrap'));
    var head  = document.querySelector('[data-ag-head]');
    function closeMegas(except){
      wraps.forEach(function(o){
        if(o!==except){ o.classList.remove('is-open'); var b=o.querySelector('[data-ag-mega-trigger]'); if(b) b.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false'); }
      });
      // The bar's hairline is removed while a panel is open (§7.1): the panel
      // hangs from the bar with no gap, and a rule between them cuts it in half.
      if(head) head.classList.toggle('is-mega', !!document.querySelector('.ag-mega-wrap.is-open'));
    }
    wraps.forEach(function(w){
      var btn=w.querySelector('[data-ag-mega-trigger]'); if(!btn) return;
      btn.addEventListener('click', function(e){
        e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
        var willOpen=!w.classList.contains('is-open');
        closeMegas(w);
        w.classList.toggle('is-open', willOpen);
        btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', willOpen?'true':'false');
        if(head) head.classList.toggle('is-mega', willOpen);
      });
      // Hover-to-open on desktop (fine pointer only) — click still works
      // everywhere, and touch devices fall through to click since they do not
      // fire hover.
      if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(hover:hover) and (pointer:fine)').matches){
        var hideT;
        w.addEventListener('mouseenter', function(){ clearTimeout(hideT); closeMegas(w); w.classList.add('is-open'); btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded','true'); if(head) head.classList.add('is-mega'); });
        w.addEventListener('mouseleave', function(){ hideT=setTimeout(function(){ w.classList.remove('is-open'); btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false'); closeMegas(null); }, 140); });
      }
    });
    document.addEventListener('click', function(e){ if(!(e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.ag-mega-wrap'))) closeMegas(null); });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e){ if(e.key==='Escape') closeMegas(null); });
  }
  if(document.readyState==='loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init); else init();
})();
</script>

